<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch December producer prices rise 2.7 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Dutch December producer prices rise 2.7 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>VOORBURG, Netherlands 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch producer price index (PPI) for manufactured goods rose a provisional 0.3 percent in December from November, giving a 2.7 percent rise year-on-year, the Central Bureau of Statistics (CBS) said.  </p>
<p> DUTCH PRODUCER PRICES	    Dec 96     Nov 96     Dec 95</p>
<p> Index (base 1990)		103.0	102.7	100.3</p>
<p> Month-on-month pct change	0.3	 -0.6	  0.3</p>
<p> Year-on-year pct change	  2.7	  2.7	  0.4</p>
<p> Subindex domestic prices     106.5	106.2	104.4</p>
<p> yr/yr pct change		   2.0	  2.0	  1.7</p>
<p> Subindex export prices	 100.3	 99.9	 97.2</p>
<p> yr/yr pct change		   3.2	  3.2	 -0.5</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
